                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14487538" author="kuaw26" created="Thu, 9 Apr 2015 15:40:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Test in branch ignite-704.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After investigation I found that it is expected behaviour.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ignite.bat and ignitevisorcmd.bat support several commandline options like &quot;-v&quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And there is special option &quot;-np&quot; that control pause or not after ignite.bat(ignitevisorcmd.bat) finished.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, I added information about this option into --help option for ignite.bat.&lt;br/&gt;
And implemented support for --help option for ignitevisorcmd.bat&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To test: execute&lt;br/&gt;
 ignite.bat --help&lt;br/&gt;
 ignitevisorcmd.bat --help&lt;br/&gt;
 ignite.bat -np&lt;br/&gt;
 ignitevisorcmd.bat -np&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="14489275" author="skozlov" created="Fri, 10 Apr 2015 09:45:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;fixed, good to merge&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14489392" author="kuaw26" created="Fri, 10 Apr 2015 11:17:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged into sprint-3. Please retest.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
